      "Match a received lot to the purchase order and the supplier's shipping documents before opening it or moving it to stores. The minimum set is a packing list, a certificate of conformance or test report, lot traceability and any special handling label. The packing list fixes what was shipped and how many units; the certificate records what the supplier tested or inspected against the purchase order; traceability links the material to a manufacturing batch, a date and a test result; the handling label shows the lot was intended for moisture, electrostatic, temperature or shelf-life control."
